The Cynics: living an argument and questioning convention (@greek-cynics: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-schools-life, #source @greek-source-diogenes, #philosophy @greek-aristotle-politics, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-aristotle-politics, #philosophy @greek-epictetus, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-epictetus, #philosophy @greek-epicurus, #ancient-greek-philosophy @greek-epicurus) { r_0R2YCT14QC77FB489JPCD107SZ
**Read:** [Diogenes Laertius, Lives and Opinions](../sources/Lives-and-Opinions-Yonge.lingua#r_2MZ8K8NBGJSS2844MJ7DDGR849), Book VI: the accounts of Antisthenes, Diogenes, Crates, and Hipparchia. Distinguish a reported practice, an anecdote, a saying, and the compiler's account of a philosophical position.

**Preparation:** [the limits of a later report](../foundations/Socrates-and-his-sources.lingua#r_1WAA32AYYPKYVETNZ5JGZ2SHFT). [Socrates' examined life](../socratic/Apology.lingua#r_0DWAPFJNVYT6WNTRT46ZVK82X4) gives a useful comparison about how conduct can express a philosophical commitment.

Ask how a practice of simplicity, frank speech, or disregard for convention could challenge an account of what makes a life good. Acting in a striking way can expose a tension in accepted values; the interpretation still needs to explain what the action demonstrates and what it assumes.

**Practice:** choose one reported action and reconstruct the claim it might be intended to support. Give a plausible alternative interpretation. For a claim of self-sufficiency, identify the material resources and other people's work on which the practice still depends.

**Check:** defend an interpretation through the source while acknowledging what an anecdote cannot establish about the historical person's life or doctrine. Compare the treatment of philosophical authority and participation in the account of Hipparchia with another passage in Book VI.

**Continue:** [Stoic agency](Epictetus.lingua#r_35EWPVCFYNWZ0DYG5R5HM05TC2), [Epicurean desire](Epicurus.lingua#r_6KHZKEFRKY1J18Z7TSRAJABZQP), or [the community and its roles](../aristotle/Political-community.lingua#r_0NZK4NKSQVX9NMTAWRT2XNBATD). **Return:** [Schools of life](Schools-of-life.lingua#r_58ENCWSNQARKCDXEP8FVWY9507) · [Ancient Greek philosophy](../Ancient-Greek-Philosophy.lingua#r_464ZHR7ZYC234A0XX2QEW47VB3).
